        <h1>LeetCode 3360: Stone Removal Game (C++)</h1>
        <div class="problem-description">
            <p><strong>Problem:</strong>
                Alice and Bob are playing a game with a pile of n stones. Alice goes first, and the players
                take turns. On the first turn, the player must remove exactly 10 stones. On each later turn,
                the player must remove exactly one fewer stone than the previous player removed (9 on Bob's
                first turn, then 8 on Alice's, and so on). A player who cannot remove the required number of
                stones loses. Return true if Alice wins the game, otherwise return false.
            </p>
            <p><strong>Example:</strong>
                Input: n = 12<br>
                Output: true<br>
                Explanation: Alice removes 10 stones, leaving 2. Bob needs to remove 9 stones but only 2
                remain, so Bob cannot move and loses.
            </p>
        </div>
        <div class="code-container">
            <button class="copy-button" onclick="copyCode(this)">Copy Code</button>
            <pre><code class="language-cpp">class Solution {
public:
    bool canAliceWin(int n) {
        int take = 10;
        while (n &gt; 0) {
            if (n &lt; take)
                return false;
            n -= take--;
            if (n &lt; take)
                return true;
            n -= take--;
        }
        return false;
    }
};</code></pre>
